      "summaries": {
        "en": "Vite+ is a unified web development toolchain that simplifies modern frontend workflows by managing runtime, package manager, and toolchain in one integrated environment. Built with Rust for performance, it offers a cohesive developer experience through a single entry point that coordinates multiple tools seamlessly. Developers can use it to streamline project setup, reduce configuration complexity, and maintain consistent tooling across different web projects, making it ideal for teams seeking efficient, standardized development pipelines.",
        "zh": "Vite+ 是一个统一的 Web 开发工具链，通过集成管理运行时、包管理器和前端工具链，简化现代前端工作流程。它采用 Rust 构建以确保高性能，并通过单一入口点协调多个工具，提供一致的开发体验。其核心设计理念是将分散的工具整合为有机整体，减少配置碎片化。开发者可用它快速搭建项目、降低工具链维护成本，特别适合需要标准化开发流程的团队，为构建现代 Web 应用提供高效起点。",
        "es": "Vite+ is a unified web development toolchain that simplifies modern frontend workflows by managing runtime, package manager, and toolchain in one integrated environment. Built with Rust for performance, it offers a cohesive developer experience through a single entry point that coordinates multiple tools seamlessly. Developers can use it to streamline project setup, reduce configuration complexity, and maintain consistent tooling across different web projects, making it ideal for teams seeking efficient, standardized development pipelines.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "vite-plus gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Vite+ is a unified web development toolchain that simplifies modern frontend workflows by managing runtime, package manager, and toolchain in one integrated environment. Built with Rust for performance, it offers a cohesive developer experience through a single entry point that coordinates multiple tools seamlessly. Developers can use it to streamline project setup, reduce configuration complexity, and maintain consistent tooling across different web projects, making it ideal for teams seeking efficient, standardized development pipelines.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/voidzero-dev/vite-plus for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
