      "summaries": {
        "en": "Project NOMAD is an offline-capable survival computing platform that provides essential tools and AI assistance without requiring internet connectivity, addressing scenarios where reliable networks are unavailable. Its technical innovation lies in bundling pre-processed knowledge bases and lightweight AI models into a portable TypeScript application that runs entirely locally. Developers can experiment by extending its modular toolset with custom survival guides or integrating alternative local AI models for specialized offline assistance tasks.",
        "zh": "Project NOMAD 是一款离线的生存计算平台，集成了关键工具和人工智能辅助功能，专门解决网络不可靠环境下的信息获取难题。其技术核心在于将预处理的知识库与轻量级AI模型打包成独立的TypeScript应用，实现完全本地化运行。通过模块化设计，开发者可以扩展自定义生存指南或集成其他本地AI模型，为户外探险、应急准备等场景构建个性化的离线智能助手。",
        "es": "Project NOMAD is an offline-capable survival computing platform that provides essential tools and AI assistance without requiring internet connectivity, addressing scenarios where reliable networks are unavailable. Its technical innovation lies in bundling pre-processed knowledge bases and lightweight AI models into a portable TypeScript application that runs entirely locally. Developers can experiment by extending its modular toolset with custom survival guides or integrating alternative local AI models for specialized offline assistance tasks.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "project-nomad gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Project NOMAD is an offline-capable survival computing platform that provides essential tools and AI assistance without requiring internet connectivity, addressing scenarios where reliable networks are unavailable. Its technical innovation lies in bundling pre-processed knowledge bases and lightweight AI models into a portable TypeScript application that runs entirely locally. Developers can experiment by extending its modular toolset with custom survival guides or integrating alternative local AI models for specialized offline assistance tasks.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Crosstalk-Solutions/project-nomad for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
